# Java imports

Use **imports and simple type names** in method bodies, parameters, and `extends`/`implements` clauses.

**Do not** spell out `org.springframework.content…` or other package paths in code when a normal import works.

**Keep a fully qualified name only when:**

- Two types share the same simple name in one file (e.g. `jakarta.persistence.Id` and
  `org.springframework.data.annotation.Id` — qualify one of them).
- The name is a string constant, annotation attribute, or framework literal that must stay qualified (e.g.
  `@MethodSource("fully.qualified.Class#method")`, package scan strings).
- Javadoc `{@link …}` or `@see` when linking to external types.

Match neighboring style: `import org.springframework.content.commons.store.*` or explicit imports, not long inline
references.